From 074d002f60f8e95bad852f864d0fa5a316a99331 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilPatrick06 <187923600+EvilPatrick06@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:21:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: list every connected gateway's scheduled jobs, and
 send each job's actions to its own gateway

The Scheduled jobs page and the sidebar's Cron jobs section asked only the
connection in front. A job on another registered connection (a Bot's
schedule on an SSH host while a chat on This device is in front) never
showed, and nothing could pause, run or edit it from there.

The all-profiles list now joins every connected registry gateway's jobs the
way the unified Sessions list joins their chats: only already-pooled
backends are read (a refresh never dials), a gateway already listed (same
connection or same install_id) is read once, and a dead one adds nothing.
Each spliced job carries the connection_id that served it, and every
per-job call (get, runs, edit, pause, resume, run now, stop, delete) goes
to that connection under the job's own profile. Rows are keyed by
(connection, id), since two gateways can hold one id.
